      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For white patients, melanoma often presents with the classic ABCDEs—asymmetry, border irregularity, color variation, diameter, and evolution—which are relatively easy to spot. In individuals with darker skin, the presentation is far more insidious; the melanoma might mimic a benign mole or look like hyperpigmentation, often appearing as a dark brown or black patch that doesn't follow the typical rules. Because of this, early detection is significantly more challenging in these populations, making the visual cues much less straightforward.",
